{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":808694,"num_turns":86,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"95634663-9c6a-4d7c-818e-b2b8c1f00fc6","total_cost_usd":5.946553500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":143654,"cache_read_input_tokens":6349051,"output_tokens":53255,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":143654,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1249,"cache_read_input_tokens":158611,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":311},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3443,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.003523,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":118,"outputTokens":53255,"cacheReadInputTokens":6349051,"cacheCreationInputTokens":143654,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":5.943030500000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Verdict: changes requested → `to-dev`.** ([artifact attached](.task-board/.resources/BUG-260731-1rldqv/BUG-260731-1rldqv_independent-review-verdict.md), notes and curator `LOGBOOK.md` updated.)\n\n## What holds\n\nI re-derived every AC claim from primary sources rather than trusting the developer report, and all of it held:\n\n- **PR 16 run `30637483316` on head `32737a8`: 14/14 green** — 12 test cells, mypy strict, Build artifacts. All three commits (`7a66c73`, `98ab7a2`, `32737a8`) carry good GPG signatures; `origin` is `ivanopcode/cocoaskills` only.\n- **Locally at `32737a8`:** mypy strict exit 0 (67 files); full suite exit 0, **1145 passed / 100 skipped**, matching the reported figure exactly.\n\nThe two load-bearing claims were testable, so I tested them instead of reading them:\n\n- **\"The guard is not weakened.\"** `32737a8` swaps an O(n²) pairwise namespace scan for three index lookups — the riskiest edit here. I copied the old algorithm verbatim out of `8a02e17` and ran it against the shipped indexed scan over identical namespace sets on a real filesystem (duplicates, containment, hardlink and symlink aliases, dangling links, absent paths, entry/bytes mixtures): **5,771 sets, zero disagreements.** The new form is in fact a superset — it indexes physical identity for every namespace, where the old code only reached that check for pairs surviving the parts checks.\n- **\"No-op on POSIX.\"** Digests persist in receipts, so I measured it: `digest_path` is **byte-identical** across the change.\n\nRoot causes are diagnosed correctly and fixed at the producer, never at the guard. The test changes are faithful to the platform rather than accommodations of it.\n\n## Why it isn't accepted\n\n`7a66c73` rewrote `csk_home.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)` as a bare `mkdir` plus `except FileExistsError: return`. **`Path.mkdir(exist_ok=True)` doesn't swallow that exception** — CPython's body is `if not exist_ok or not self.is_dir(): raise`. The bare `except` discards that type check, so a non-directory at the manager-home path is now accepted:\n\n| `~/.cocoaskills` is | `8a02e17` | `32737a8` |\n|---|---|---|\n| symlink → **missing** dir | `LockError` | **home created at the link destination, mode `0o755`, never provisioned** |\n| a regular file | `LockError` | raw `FileExistsError` escapes `cli.main` |\n\nThat skips both the `0o700` create mode and, on Windows, the entire ownership/DACL stamp this commit exists to apply — inside the very function it added to establish that state.\n\nI checked reachability rather than assuming it: **it's latent, not live.** Every `GlobalLock(cfg.path.parent)` site is preceded by `config.load_config()`, which fails first, and `csk bootstrap` already died on this input before the change. It's still rework — the task scope names ownership guards explicitly, `provision_new_manager_home` was newly promoted to a public two-caller function, and no test covers the case. Fix is two lines plus a test.\n\nAlso routed: `32737a8`'s cost contract is unpinned (a pairwise scan over memoised probes would leave both cost tests green), and the curator logbook entry stopped at `7a66c73`.\n\nRework is bounded and autonomous — nothing needs a human decision, and nothing in the Windows fix or its evidence needs redoing.","ttft_ms":2050,"ttft_stream_ms":1533,"time_to_request_ms":75,"type":"result","duration_ms":929359,"uuid":"f92df6d3-deaf-498a-8270-3ad84f037dcb"}
